1
00:00:02,258 --> 00:00:03,885
KATARA: Water.

2
00:00:04,844 --> 00:00:06,221
Earth.

3
00:00:06,804 --> 00:00:08,223
Fire.

4
00:00:08,890 --> 00:00:10,517
Air.

5
00:00:11,351 --> 00:00:14,604
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

6
00:00:15,271 --> 00:00:18,566
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

7
00:00:19,609 --> 00:00:22,570
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

8
00:00:22,654 --> 00:00:23,863
could stop them.

9
00:00:23,947 --> 00:00:26,866
But when the world
needed him most, he vanished.

10
00:00:27,242 --> 00:00:28,368
A hundred years passed,

11
00:00:28,451 --> 00:00:30,870
and my brother and I
discovered the new Avatar,

12
00:00:30,954 --> 00:00:32,705
an airbender named Aang.

13
00:00:32,914 --> 00:00:35,041
And although his
airbending skills are great,

14
00:00:35,124 --> 00:00:37,710
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

15
00:00:37,794 --> 00:00:38,795
AANG: Oof.

16
00:00:38,878 --> 00:00:41,839
But I believe
Aang can save the world.

17
00:00:47,845 --> 00:00:50,056
ROKU: Previously on Avatar...

18
00:00:50,348 --> 00:00:53,643
KATARA: I can't believe we finally made it
to Ba Sing Se in one piece.

19
00:00:53,893 --> 00:00:59,774
I just want our new place to look nice,
in case someone brings home a lady friend.

20
00:00:59,857 --> 00:01:01,859
ZUKO: I don't want to make a life here.

21
00:01:02,068 --> 00:01:04,445
JOO DEE: Here we are,
your new home.

22
00:01:05,113 --> 00:01:07,073
We need to talk to the king
about the war.

23
00:01:07,156 --> 00:01:10,660
Your request for an audience
with the Earth King is being processed,

24
00:01:10,743 --> 00:01:12,787
and should be put through
in about a month!

25
00:01:13,162 --> 00:01:16,833
If we're gonna be here for a month,
we should spend our time looking for Appa.

26
00:01:36,728 --> 00:01:37,770
( CLICKING TONGUE )

27
00:01:41,482 --> 00:01:42,734
( CHIRPING )

28
00:01:45,612 --> 00:01:46,863
( GASPING )

29
00:01:46,946 --> 00:01:49,073
Toph, aren't you
gonna get ready for the day?

30
00:01:51,618 --> 00:01:52,702
( HOCKING AND SPITTING )

31
00:01:56,122 --> 00:01:57,206
I'm ready.

32
00:01:57,290 --> 00:01:58,833
You're not gonna wash up?

33
00:01:58,916 --> 00:02:02,253
You've got a little dirt on your...
Everywhere, actually.

34
00:02:02,670 --> 00:02:06,466
You call it dirt, I call it
a healthy coating of earth.

35
00:02:06,549 --> 00:02:07,675
Hmm...

36
00:02:07,759 --> 00:02:09,135
You know what we need?

37
00:02:09,469 --> 00:02:11,429
A girls' day out!

38
00:02:11,804 --> 00:02:13,264
Do I have to?

39
00:02:13,348 --> 00:02:14,891
KATARA: It'll be fun.

40
00:02:19,103 --> 00:02:21,189
TOPH: The Fancy Lady Day Spa?

41
00:02:21,272 --> 00:02:23,149
Sounds like my kind of place.

42
00:02:23,608 --> 00:02:25,902
Are you ready for
some serious pampering?

43
00:02:26,569 --> 00:02:28,237
( HESITATING ) Sure, Katara.

44
00:02:28,321 --> 00:02:29,781
Whatever you say.

45
00:02:29,864 --> 00:02:31,699
As long as
they don't touch my feet.

46
00:02:36,829 --> 00:02:37,830
( SCRAPING )

47
00:02:38,206 --> 00:02:40,166
( GRUNTING AND GROWLING )

48
00:02:41,668 --> 00:02:42,710
Ugh!

49
00:02:42,794 --> 00:02:43,795
Uh...

50
00:02:49,050 --> 00:02:50,968
( BLOWING )

51
00:02:52,053 --> 00:02:53,763
( SCREAMING )

52
00:02:54,347 --> 00:02:56,808
( BOTH LAUGHING )

53
00:03:03,064 --> 00:03:04,857
( BOTH SIGHING )

54
00:03:07,110 --> 00:03:08,820
Well, that wasn't so bad.

55
00:03:09,070 --> 00:03:13,449
I'm not usually into that stuff,
but I actually feel... Girly.

56
00:03:13,700 --> 00:03:14,742
KATARA: I'm glad.

57
00:03:14,826 --> 00:03:16,994
It's about time
we did something fun together.

58
00:03:22,333 --> 00:03:24,001
Wow, great makeup.

59
00:03:24,085 --> 00:03:25,086
Thanks.

60
00:03:25,253 --> 00:03:26,504
For a clown.

61
00:03:27,004 --> 00:03:29,382
( LAUGHING )

62
00:03:30,216 --> 00:03:32,385
Don't listen to them.
Let's just keep walking.

63
00:03:32,719 --> 00:03:34,512
I think she looks cute.

64
00:03:34,595 --> 00:03:37,473
Like that time we put a sweater
on your pet poodle-monkey.

65
00:03:37,557 --> 00:03:39,726
( LAUGHTER )

66
00:03:40,727 --> 00:03:41,936
GIRL: Good one, Star.

67
00:03:42,520 --> 00:03:43,896
Let's go, Toph.

68
00:03:44,021 --> 00:03:46,691
TOPH: No, no,
that was a good one.

69
00:03:46,774 --> 00:03:48,192
"Like your poodle-monkey."

70
00:03:48,276 --> 00:03:49,986
( LAUGHING )

71
00:03:50,069 --> 00:03:51,863
You, you know what else
is a good one?

72
00:03:53,114 --> 00:03:54,115
( SCREAMING )

73
00:03:56,159 --> 00:03:57,744
Now that was funny.

74
00:03:58,953 --> 00:04:00,204
( SCREAMING )

75
00:04:00,747 --> 00:04:03,082
Those girls don't know what
they're talking about.

76
00:04:03,374 --> 00:04:04,542
TOPH: It's okay.

77
00:04:04,625 --> 00:04:06,502
One of the good things
about being blind

78
00:04:06,586 --> 00:04:09,881
Is that I don't have to waste my time
worrying about appearances.

79
00:04:09,964 --> 00:04:11,841
I don't care what I look like.

80
00:04:11,924 --> 00:04:14,093
I'm not looking for
anyone's approval.

81
00:04:14,594 --> 00:04:16,220
I know who I am.

82
00:04:16,304 --> 00:04:18,765
KATARA: That's what
I really admire about you, Toph.

83
00:04:19,098 --> 00:04:21,768
You're so strong and confident
and self-assured.

84
00:04:22,059 --> 00:04:23,186
( SNIFFING )

85
00:04:23,269 --> 00:04:25,438
And I know
it doesn't matter, but...

86
00:04:25,688 --> 00:04:27,190
You're really pretty.

87
00:04:27,690 --> 00:04:28,733
I am?

88
00:04:29,025 --> 00:04:30,401
Yeah, you are.

89
00:04:34,906 --> 00:04:38,409
TOPH: I'd return the compliment,
but I have no idea what you look like.

90
00:04:38,493 --> 00:04:39,702
( KATARA LAUGHING )

91
00:04:39,786 --> 00:04:40,995
TOPH: Thank you, Katara.

92
00:04:41,078 --> 00:04:42,163
KATARA: Ow!

93
00:04:55,760 --> 00:04:59,972
If this is for a romantic picnic,
may I suggest this lavender one?

94
00:05:00,056 --> 00:05:05,228
No, it's not a romantic picnic,
but it is a special occasion.

95
00:05:13,611 --> 00:05:16,572
IROH: The moonflower
likes partial shade.

96
00:05:24,163 --> 00:05:25,456
( CHILD CRYING )

97
00:05:25,540 --> 00:05:27,750
WOMAN: It's okay, Shh, shh, shh.

98
00:05:27,834 --> 00:05:29,877
WOMAN: It's okay, Shh.

99
00:05:31,170 --> 00:05:33,631
( MUSIC PLAYING )

100
00:05:34,382 --> 00:05:37,510
♪ Leaves from the vine

101
00:05:37,635 --> 00:05:40,137
♪ Falling so slow

102
00:05:40,263 --> 00:05:47,103
♪ Like fragile, tiny shells
drifting in the foam

103
00:05:47,478 --> 00:05:53,734
♪ Little soldier boy,
come marching home

104
00:05:54,110 --> 00:05:57,154
♪ Brave soldier boy

105
00:05:59,657 --> 00:06:03,244
♪ Comes marching home ♪

106
00:06:05,621 --> 00:06:06,956
Yeowch!

107
00:06:07,039 --> 00:06:08,332
( LAUGHING )

108
00:06:24,599 --> 00:06:26,225
MAN: Hey!

109
00:06:26,309 --> 00:06:29,645
IROH: It is usually best to
admit mistakes when they occur.

110
00:06:30,021 --> 00:06:32,148
And to seek to restore honor.

111
00:06:32,231 --> 00:06:34,150
( STOMPING )

112
00:06:34,233 --> 00:06:38,905
When I'm through with you kids, the window
won't be the only thing that's broken!

113
00:06:39,030 --> 00:06:40,489
But not this time.

114
00:06:40,573 --> 00:06:41,657
Run!

115
00:06:49,624 --> 00:06:50,875
THIEF: You.

116
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:52,710
Give me all your money!

117
00:06:56,047 --> 00:06:57,673
What are you doing?

118
00:06:57,757 --> 00:06:58,966
I'm mugging you!

119
00:06:59,050 --> 00:07:00,426
With that stance?

120
00:07:00,509 --> 00:07:01,636
Wha-?

121
00:07:01,719 --> 00:07:03,095
What are you talking about?

122
00:07:03,179 --> 00:07:04,805
Just give me your money,
old man!

123
00:07:05,181 --> 00:07:10,227
With a poor stance, you are unbalanced,
and you can be easily knocked over.

124
00:07:12,480 --> 00:07:13,481
Ugh!

125
00:07:18,736 --> 00:07:23,532
With a solid stance, you are
a much more serious threat.

126
00:07:27,370 --> 00:07:28,621
Much better!

127
00:07:28,996 --> 00:07:33,250
But to tell you the truth,
you do not look like the criminal type.

128
00:07:33,626 --> 00:07:35,294
I know, I'm...

129
00:07:35,628 --> 00:07:36,796
I'm just confused.

130
00:07:39,298 --> 00:07:41,801
THIEF: So you really think
I could be a good masseur?

131
00:07:41,884 --> 00:07:43,177
Of course!

132
00:07:44,845 --> 00:07:46,097
This is so great!

133
00:07:46,722 --> 00:07:48,265
No one has ever believed in me.

134
00:07:48,724 --> 00:07:52,061
While it is always best
to believe in oneself,

135
00:07:52,144 --> 00:07:56,148
a little help from others
can be a great blessing.

136
00:08:20,631 --> 00:08:22,800
IROH: Happy birthday, my son.

137
00:08:24,677 --> 00:08:27,471
If only I could have helped you.

138
00:08:28,806 --> 00:08:32,059
♪ Leaves from the vine

139
00:08:32,935 --> 00:08:35,438
♪ Falling so slow

140
00:08:35,521 --> 00:08:41,986
♪ Like fragile, tiny shells
drifting in the foam

141
00:08:42,570 --> 00:08:46,323
( CRYING ) ♪ Little soldier boy

142
00:08:46,407 --> 00:08:48,117
♪ Come marching home

143
00:08:49,201 --> 00:08:52,872
♪ Brave soldier boy

144
00:08:52,997 --> 00:08:56,584
♪ Comes marching home ♪

145
00:09:35,081 --> 00:09:36,207
Hey there, fella.

146
00:09:36,582 --> 00:09:37,666
AANG: You look hungry.

147
00:09:37,750 --> 00:09:38,751
Ahh!

148
00:09:42,338 --> 00:09:43,464
They are hungry.

149
00:09:45,883 --> 00:09:49,178
The Dai Li won't give me any money
because the kids stopped coming.

150
00:09:49,595 --> 00:09:52,681
And the kids won't come because
my zoo's nasty and broke.

151
00:09:53,265 --> 00:09:54,683
What kind of animal is that?

152
00:09:54,934 --> 00:09:56,227
Ooh, that's a rabbiroo.

153
00:09:56,310 --> 00:09:59,188
I wish I could get her a big,
open prairie, like she likes.

154
00:10:00,022 --> 00:10:01,774
I'd let her
hop her way to happiness.

155
00:10:04,026 --> 00:10:06,028
- Let's do it.
- Say again?

156
00:10:06,112 --> 00:10:09,031
There's a big open space right
outside the walls of the city.

157
00:10:09,115 --> 00:10:12,284
ZOOKEEPER: But how are you
gonna transport all these wild critters?

158
00:10:12,368 --> 00:10:14,370
Don't worry,
I'm great with animals.

159
00:10:22,920 --> 00:10:25,214
( SCREAMING )

160
00:10:32,805 --> 00:10:34,807
( SPUTTERING )

161
00:10:35,474 --> 00:10:37,101
My cab-

162
00:10:38,227 --> 00:10:39,812
Oh, forget it.

163
00:10:40,437 --> 00:10:42,898
( SCREAMING )

164
00:10:52,032 --> 00:10:54,243
This was so much easier
in my head.

165
00:10:59,248 --> 00:11:00,374
( INHALING )

166
00:11:15,097 --> 00:11:16,098
( CRYING )

167
00:11:23,105 --> 00:11:25,024
Oom-oom-oom, oom-oom-oom.

168
00:11:25,858 --> 00:11:27,568
But you have to open this gate!

169
00:11:27,651 --> 00:11:28,736
Or what?

170
00:11:28,819 --> 00:11:29,820
Or that!

171
00:11:33,574 --> 00:11:35,159
Open the gate!

172
00:12:10,194 --> 00:12:12,571
( GRUNTING )

173
00:12:21,413 --> 00:12:22,665
( LAUGHING )

174
00:12:30,297 --> 00:12:31,632
( SQUEAKING )

175
00:12:32,258 --> 00:12:35,302
Well, Mr. Zookeeper, how do you
like your new facilities?

176
00:12:35,386 --> 00:12:37,513
Excellent job, Avatar.

177
00:12:37,596 --> 00:12:40,266
You should think about working
with animals for a living.

178
00:12:40,349 --> 00:12:43,435
CHILD 1: Mommy, Miss Snowflake
got out of the house again.

179
00:12:43,519 --> 00:12:44,812
( HISSING )

180
00:12:44,895 --> 00:12:47,314
CHILD 2: Fluffikins, what are you
doing down there?

181
00:12:47,398 --> 00:12:48,983
( MEOWING )

182
00:12:49,066 --> 00:12:52,194
On second thought, you should
probably stick to saving people.

183
00:12:52,278 --> 00:12:54,530
( LAUGHING NERVOUSLY )

184
00:13:10,337 --> 00:13:12,256
( ANIMAL GRUNTING )

185
00:13:12,965 --> 00:13:14,383
( FAINT CONVERSATION )

186
00:13:15,384 --> 00:13:16,593
What's this?

187
00:13:16,677 --> 00:13:18,554
"Through all the long night,

188
00:13:18,637 --> 00:13:21,432
"Winter moon glows
with bright love.

189
00:13:21,515 --> 00:13:24,018
"Sleet, her silver tears."

190
00:13:24,476 --> 00:13:27,229
Ahh, poetry.

191
00:13:27,313 --> 00:13:28,856
( GRUNTING )

192
00:13:28,939 --> 00:13:30,149
Augh!

193
00:13:30,232 --> 00:13:31,233
( WOMEN GASPING )

194
00:13:32,735 --> 00:13:34,278
I am so sorry.

195
00:13:34,945 --> 00:13:36,739
Something struck me in the rear.

196
00:13:37,740 --> 00:13:41,118
I just... Wound up... Here?

197
00:13:41,493 --> 00:13:46,248
( LAUGHING )

198
00:13:48,459 --> 00:13:54,381
"Five, seven, then five syllables mark
a haiku, remarkable oaf."

199
00:13:57,384 --> 00:14:03,640
"They call me Sokka, that is,
in the water tribe. I am not an oaf."

200
00:14:03,807 --> 00:14:06,226
( LAUGHING )

201
00:14:06,477 --> 00:14:12,441
"Chittering monkey. In the spring he
climbs treetops and thinks himself tall."

202
00:14:12,900 --> 00:14:14,443
Ooh...

203
00:14:14,777 --> 00:14:19,782
"You think you're so smart, with your
fancy little words. This is not so hard."

204
00:14:20,240 --> 00:14:22,117
WOMEN: Ooh...

205
00:14:22,326 --> 00:14:27,623
"Whole seasons are spent mastering
the form, the style. None calls it easy."

206
00:14:27,706 --> 00:14:33,128
"I calls it easy. Like I paddle my canoe,
I'll paddle yours, too."

207
00:14:33,462 --> 00:14:36,840
( LAUGHING )

208
00:14:37,299 --> 00:14:40,010
"There's nuts and there's fruits.

209
00:14:40,094 --> 00:14:44,473
"In fall, the clean plum drops,
always to be squashed."

210
00:14:46,975 --> 00:14:49,311
"Squish-squash sling that slang,

211
00:14:49,395 --> 00:14:53,524
"I'm always right back at ya,
like my... Boomerang."

212
00:14:53,857 --> 00:14:56,485
( LAUGHING )

213
00:15:00,864 --> 00:15:04,535
"That's right, I'm Sokka,
it's pronounced with an 'Okka,

214
00:15:04,618 --> 00:15:07,496
"'young ladies, I rocked ya."

215
00:15:10,332 --> 00:15:11,333
( CRICKET CHIRPING )

216
00:15:15,712 --> 00:15:19,133
Uh, that's one too many
syllables there, bub.

217
00:15:22,594 --> 00:15:23,595
Augh!

218
00:15:26,807 --> 00:15:27,933
Poetry.

219
00:15:40,404 --> 00:15:42,573
Uncle, we have a problem.

220
00:15:43,699 --> 00:15:45,451
One of the customers
is on to us.

221
00:15:46,243 --> 00:15:49,413
Don't look now, but there is
a girl over there at the corner table.

222
00:15:49,496 --> 00:15:51,123
ZUKO: She knows we're Fire Nation.

223
00:15:51,999 --> 00:15:53,667
Didn't I say don't look?

224
00:15:54,126 --> 00:15:55,544
IROH: You're right, Zuko.

225
00:15:55,627 --> 00:15:58,088
I've seen that girl in here quite a lot.

226
00:15:58,547 --> 00:16:02,092
Seems to me she has
quite a little crush on you.

227
00:16:02,176 --> 00:16:03,177
What?

228
00:16:03,260 --> 00:16:04,761
Thank you for the tea.

229
00:16:06,597 --> 00:16:07,806
What's your name?

230
00:16:08,307 --> 00:16:09,600
My name's Lee.

231
00:16:09,683 --> 00:16:11,185
My uncle and I just moved here.

232
00:16:11,602 --> 00:16:14,104
Hi, Lee, my name's Jin.

233
00:16:14,188 --> 00:16:16,106
Thank you, and, well,

234
00:16:16,690 --> 00:16:19,985
I was wondering if you would
like to go out some time.

235
00:16:20,068 --> 00:16:21,278
He'd love to.

236
00:16:21,653 --> 00:16:24,323
Great! I'll meet you
in front of the shop at sundown.

237
00:16:37,377 --> 00:16:38,504
Hey.

238
00:16:38,587 --> 00:16:40,088
Well, look at you.

239
00:16:40,422 --> 00:16:41,798
You look so cute.

240
00:16:42,257 --> 00:16:45,219
It took my uncle
ten minutes to do my hair.

241
00:16:50,057 --> 00:16:52,684
So, how do you
like the city so far?

242
00:16:52,768 --> 00:16:53,977
It's okay.

243
00:16:54,394 --> 00:16:55,979
What do you like to do for fun?

244
00:16:56,063 --> 00:16:57,356
Nothing.

245
00:16:57,439 --> 00:17:00,400
Excuse me, sir, would you
and your girlfriend care for dessert?

246
00:17:00,484 --> 00:17:02,277
( SCREAMING ) She is not my girlfriend!

247
00:17:08,200 --> 00:17:12,204
You have...
Quite an appetite for a girl.

248
00:17:12,579 --> 00:17:14,373
Um, thanks?

249
00:17:15,832 --> 00:17:20,295
So, Lee, where were you and your uncle
living before you came here?

250
00:17:20,420 --> 00:17:25,259
( HESITATING ) Um, well, we've been
traveling around for a long time.

251
00:17:25,342 --> 00:17:27,928
Oh! Why were you traveling so much?

252
00:17:28,011 --> 00:17:31,473
We were, uh, part of this
traveling circus.

253
00:17:31,557 --> 00:17:32,724
Really?

254
00:17:32,808 --> 00:17:34,893
What did you do?
Wait, let me guess.

255
00:17:35,769 --> 00:17:36,770
You juggled.

256
00:17:38,105 --> 00:17:39,606
Yes, I juggled.

257
00:17:39,690 --> 00:17:41,650
I've always wanted to
learn how to juggle.

258
00:17:41,733 --> 00:17:43,068
Can you show me something?

259
00:17:46,154 --> 00:17:47,447
Uh...

260
00:17:49,783 --> 00:17:51,118
Whoa, uh!

261
00:17:51,660 --> 00:17:53,453
I haven't practiced for a while.

262
00:17:53,537 --> 00:17:54,955
JIN: It's all right.

263
00:17:55,789 --> 00:17:59,376
Hey, I want to show you
one of my favorite places in the city.

264
00:18:00,627 --> 00:18:03,380
JIN: I'm so excited for you
to see the firelight fountain.

265
00:18:03,463 --> 00:18:05,090
The lamps make the water sparkle,

266
00:18:05,173 --> 00:18:08,135
and reflect in the pool
in the most beautiful way.

267
00:18:10,512 --> 00:18:11,722
I can't believe it!

268
00:18:11,805 --> 00:18:13,015
JIN: They aren't lit.

269
00:18:16,893 --> 00:18:17,894
Close your eyes.

270
00:18:17,978 --> 00:18:18,979
And don't peek.

271
00:18:37,080 --> 00:18:39,291
ZUKO: Okay, Now you can look.

272
00:18:39,750 --> 00:18:41,585
Oh, wow...

273
00:18:45,213 --> 00:18:46,298
What happened?

274
00:18:46,381 --> 00:18:47,633
How did they light?

275
00:18:47,716 --> 00:18:49,051
What did you...

276
00:18:59,936 --> 00:19:01,438
I brought you something.

277
00:19:01,772 --> 00:19:03,982
ZUKO: It's a coupon
for a free cup of tea.

278
00:19:04,399 --> 00:19:06,943
Lee, this is so sweet.

279
00:19:07,903 --> 00:19:09,738
Don't thank me,
it was my uncle's idea.

280
00:19:09,821 --> 00:19:11,907
He thinks you're our
most valuable customer.

281
00:19:11,990 --> 00:19:13,617
Your uncle is a good teacher.

282
00:19:15,369 --> 00:19:17,496
I have something for you, too.

283
00:19:17,579 --> 00:19:19,998
Now it's your turn
to close your eyes.

284
00:19:27,798 --> 00:19:28,840
JIN: What's wrong?

285
00:19:29,341 --> 00:19:30,509
It's complicated.

286
00:19:30,592 --> 00:19:31,593
I have to go.

287
00:19:43,730 --> 00:19:45,565
How was your night, Prince Zuko?

288
00:19:50,654 --> 00:19:51,655
It was nice.

